Z||000004||Patrick's Dad||07-26-2001||10:41 AM||||Galen, good article, even though (now that I'm out of the 18-35 bracket by 12 days) you had to <I>swear</I> so many times in it (joke).<P>A local commentator puts it simply. Those in front of the camera (i.e. Jesse Jackson, Patricia Ireland, or the gay equivalent) used the term "racist" or "racism," and they expect everyone to kowtow to their private definition of the word, despite the fact that they are blatantly racist themselves. In other words, even though "racism" means something specific and agreed upon by society at large, and so defined by Websters, for instance, each time it is used by a "minority leader," the meaning is perverted to mean "those people who, by default, are against us."<P>We all need to grow up and learn that "equal" does not mean "we are better or more deserving than you."||||reg||1
